  "notes": "Built from the archived 2022-23 bulletin (bulletins.psu.edu/archive/2022-2023/undergraduate/colleges/health-human-development/health-policy-administration-bs/), cross-checked raw HTML against the page's own printed semester credit subtotals (14/15/16/15/15/15+3-summer/15/12, total 119-121) -- confirmed internally consistent, no WebFetch-style confabulation found. Real differences from the 2026 plan, all confirmed against the archived page directly: (1) HPA 200 ('An Introduction to Data in the Health Care System') did not exist yet -- 0 occurrences anywhere on the 2022-23 page, including the department's own course-list table; it isn't in this plan at all, unlike 2026's Semester 4. (2) The 'Select 9 credits' 400-level elective pool for the major (Requirements for the Major, Additional Courses) was smaller: HPA 438 (Culturally Competent Health Services for Diverse Populations) and HPA 446 (Economics and Health In Low- and Middle-Income Countries) are both entirely absent from the 2022-23 bulletin (0 occurrences), i.e. they hadn't been created as courses yet, not just left out of the pool. Since 2026's plan uses HPA 446 as its third required 400-level elective (paired with STAT 200/ECON 102 prereqs already scheduled), and HPA 446 didn't exist in 2022, substituted HPA 447 (Financing Health Care) instead -- confirmed real for 2022-23 (present in that year's pool) and its own real prereq (HPA 332 + HPA 211, per Backend/catalogs/hpa_catalog.json) is satisfied by Semester 3-4 in this plan, same 'resolves cleanly' logic the 2026 plan's notes already use for its own choices. HPA 442 and HPA 444 (this plan's other two required 400-level electives) were both already real, pool-listed courses in 2022-23, so kept as-is. (3) The course SEQUENCE differs from 2026's, not just the course list: HPA 301W sits in Semester 3 (2022-23) vs Semester 4 (2026); HPA 311/HPA 332 sit in Semester 4 (2022-23) vs split across Semester 4/6 (2026); HPA 390W sits in Semester 6 (2022-23) vs Semester 4 (2026); the CMPSC/MIS item sits in Semester 4 (2022-23) vs Semester 5 (2026); and the extra 'GEN ED (Arts)' course that 2026 schedules in Semester 1 is instead a pair of GEN ED (Arts) courses in Semester 5 here, matching the archived page's own Third Year Fall row -- all rebuilt to match the 2022-23 page's own Suggested Academic Plan table row-by-row, not assumed identical to 2026. (4) 'HPA 395' (Field Experience, a Summer course on the printed page) is folded into Semester 6 alongside the rest of that year's Spring-term items, same engine-pacing convention the 2026 plan's own notes describe (credits, not literal term labels, drive scheduling). Everything else -- ECON 102/HPA 101/HPA 210/HPA 211/HPA 310/HPA 332/HPA 455/PLSC 1 as C-required Prescribed Courses, the CMPSC 101/203/MIS 204 and STAT 200/250 Additional-Courses choices, the 30-credit Supporting Courses and Related Areas requirement (9 credits at 400-level) -- is unchanged from 2026 and confirmed present, word-for-word, on the 2022-23 archived page. Same STAT 200/250->STAT 100 MATH-21-prereq-chain fallback and CMPSC 203-over-CMPSC-101 substitution as 2026's plan, since those are driven by this app's current (not year-versioned) course-catalog prereq data (Backend/catalogs/), same convention CMPSC-2022.json already uses. The generic 'Supporting Course' (30-credit, department-list) and 'Supporting Course (400-level)' pools are carried over from 2026's plan (sourced from the live, non-archived hhd.psu.edu/hpa/supporting-courses department page, so not independently re-verified per catalog year) with HPA 438, HPA 446, HPA 447 (now separately required above), and HPA 494H excluded from the 400-level pool for this year specifically, since none of those four are confirmed to have existed as HPA courses in 2022-23.",
